 "arc": "A slow four-count dip: the body sinks and rises through the knees while the hips push out to one side. Anticipation is a light lift onto the balls of both feet, the action is both knees bending as the weight drops and the character-left hip presses out, and the recovery is a smooth press back up through the legs. The dip is in the legs and pelvis — the torso stays tall the whole way down.\n\nArms ride the dip passively at waist-to-chest height, elbows bent, drifting up a little as the body rises. The head stays level; do not let it drop with the hips.\n\nLoop seam: the cycle closes at the top of the rise, both feet under the body, so frame 15 flows straight into frame 0 with no landing to hold.",
